From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] orch: complete cancelled commands independently

When a duplicate WSC M1 arrives, remove_em_config_cmd_for_em() cancels the
radio's current em_config command before the controller submits the new M2
transaction.  It sets the candidate to em_orch_state_cancel, but orchestrate()
only handles pending, progress and fini.  The cancelled candidate therefore
never completes, never returns to idle and permanently prevents the replacement
em_config command from becoming active.

The controller-side workaround forced wsc_m2_sent radios directly to
topo_sync_pending from a sibling's state machine.  Live traces showed it firing
0.6-5 ms after M2, proving it was bypassing this orchestration deadlock rather
than recovering a timed-out radio.

Treat cancel as a terminal orchestration state.  Also compute completion per
active command: the old accumulator retained a false result from one command
while inspecting every later command, so an unrelated incomplete transaction
could prevent a fully-finished command from being retired.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/orch/em_orch.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/orch/em_orch.cpp b/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
--- a/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch.cpp
@@ -336,6 +336,8 @@ bool em_orch_t::orchestrate(em_cmd_t *pcmd, em_t *em)
     } else if (orch_state == em_orch_state_fini) {
         // em_printfout("em:%s Detected in fini state", mac_str);
         done = true;
+    } else if (orch_state == em_orch_state_cancel) {
+        done = true;
     }
 
     return done;
@@ -517,7 +519,6 @@ void em_orch_t::handle_timeout()
     signed int i, j; 
     unsigned int cnt;
     bool eligible_to_move = false;
-    bool ret = true;
 
     // go through pending queue and check if the commands can be moved to active
     for (i = static_cast<int>(queue_count(m_pending)) - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
@@ -554,6 +555,7 @@ void em_orch_t::handle_timeout()
     // go through active queue and check command states
     for (i = static_cast<int>(queue_count(m_active)) - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
         pcmd = static_cast<em_cmd_t *>(queue_peek(m_active, static_cast<unsigned int>(i)));
+        bool ret = true;
 		//printf("%s:%d: Cmd: %s, em candidates: %d\n", __func__, __LINE__, 
 					//em_cmd_t::get_cmd_type_str(pcmd->m_type), queue_count(pcmd->m_em_candidates));
         for (j = static_cast<int>(queue_count(pcmd->m_em_candidates)) - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
